post_install() {
  cat <<'EOF'
browse is installed at /usr/bin/browse; the relay binary lives in
/usr/lib/opencode-browse.

The Chrome extension is not part of this package. Install it from the Chrome
Web Store:
  https://chromewebstore.google.com/detail/mfnicocicmmlkpjnaffgihfjhdgjkdjg
Each browser profile pairs once with `browse pair`.

To use browse as an MCP server, add it to your agent's configuration, for
example in ~/.config/opencode/opencode.json:

  "browse": { "type": "local", "command": ["browse", "mcp"] }

Do not run `browse install`: for a binary install it copies itself to
~/.local/bin, and that copy updates itself outside pacman. If a copy from the
install script is still there, delete ~/.local/bin/browse and point your MCP
configuration at /usr/bin/browse.

The wrapper disables browse's automatic updates because pacman owns this
install. Update with `pacman -Syu`.
EOF
}

post_upgrade() {
  post_install
}
